====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[breastfeed]]: to [[feed#Verb|feed]] (a baby) at the [[breast]]; to [[suckle]].
#: ''She believes that '''nursing''' her baby will make him strong and healthy''.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[breastfeed]]: to be [[feed|fed]] at the [[breast]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[care for]] (someone), especially in [[sickness]]; to [[tend]] to.
#: {{ux|en|She '''nursed''' him back to health.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To tend gently and with extra care.
#: {{ux|en|She '''nursed''' the rosebush and that season it bloomed.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To manage or oversee (something) with care and [[economy]].
#: {{synonyms|en|husband#Verb}}
# {{senseid|en|drink}} {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[drink#Verb|drink]] (a beverage) slowly, so as to make it last.
#: {{ux|en|Rob was '''nursing''' a small beer.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To [[foster#Verb|foster]], [[nourish]], or [[entertain]] (an attitude, usually [[negative]]) in one's mind.
#: {{co|en|to '''nurse''' a grudge}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020-04-10|author=Stephen Buranyi|title=The WHO v coronavirus: why it can't handle the pandemic|journal=w:The Guardian|titleurl=https://www.theguardian.com/news/2020/apr/10/world-health-organization-who-v-coronavirus-why-it-cant-handle-pandemic|passage=If, like me, you have been confined to your home, glued to the news and '''nursing''' ever greater anxiety about the state of the world, you have probably become familiar with the sight of the {{w|World Health Organization}}’s director general, {{w|Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus}}, and his daily press briefings.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To hold closely to one's [[chest]].
#: {{ux|en|Would you like to '''nurse''' the puppy?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|billiards}} To [[strike#Verb|strike]] (billiard balls) [[gently]], so as to keep them in good [[position#Noun|position]] during a series of [[shot#Noun|shot]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1866|author=United States. Congress. Joint Committee on the Conduct of the War|title=Supplemental report of the Joint Committee
|passage=It is to our interest to let Lee and Johnston come together, just as a billiard-player would '''nurse''' the balls when he has them in a nice place}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In {{senseno|en|drink}} “to drink slowly”, generally negative and particularly used for someone at a [[bar#Noun|bar]], suggesting they either cannot afford to buy another drink or are too [[miserly]] to do so. By contrast, {{m|en|sip}} is more [[neutral#Adjective|neutral]].

